## Configuration

Copy `.env.example` to `.env`. The generated example is the complete Env contract for this project's selected features.

Brand identity lives in `internal/brand`. The framework, database, mailer, payment provider, and included modules live in generated Go source. Env contains only deployment coordinates, external IDs, operator switches, and secrets.
{{- if .API }}

## JSON API

The API lives under `/api/v1`. Its OpenAPI 3.1 document is `internal/api/openapi.yaml`, served at `/api/v1/openapi.yaml`. Sign in with an `/api/v1/auth` endpoint and send the token as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Set `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` to the browser origins that may call the API.

Users create personal API tokens {{ if .IsHeadless }}with `POST /api/v1/account/tokens`{{ else }}under Settings, Security, or with `POST /api/v1/account/tokens`{{ end }}. A token is shown once, has the `read` scope or `read` and `write`{{ if .Workspaces }}, is bound to one workspace{{ end }}, and works only on the operations whose `openapi.yaml` entry lists `apiTokenAuth`.
{{- if .IsSvelte }}

The SvelteKit app uses the same API on the same origin. It signs in with `?session=cookie`, so the session lives in an HttpOnly cookie and the app never stores a token. `APP_URL` is the URL of this server, and emails link to the app's pages under `APP_URL/auth/...`.
{{- else if not .HasHTMLFrontend }}

`APP_URL` is the URL of your frontend. Emails link to `APP_URL/auth/...`, and your frontend calls the matching `/api/v1/auth/.../verify` endpoint with the token from the link.
{{- if .OAuth }}

OAuth sign-in starts at `API_URL/auth/{provider}`, returns to `API_URL/auth/{provider}/callback`, and ends at `APP_URL/app` with a session cookie for the `API_URL` host. `API_URL` defaults to `APP_URL`. When they differ, both must share a site, for example `app.example.com` and `api.example.com`.
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
